  "content": {
    "id": "p6-problem-5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "[Thin lens equation]\n\nConsider the equation\n\n$$\\frac{1}{u}+\\frac{1}{v}=\\frac{1}{f}.$$",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-problem-5-part-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $u=\\dfrac{vf}{v-f}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$u=\\dfrac{vf}{v-f}$.\n\nSubtract $\\dfrac{1}{v}$, use a common denominator and take the reciprocal.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{u}&=\\frac{1}{f}-\\frac{1}{v}\\\\\\frac{1}{u}&=\\frac{v-f}{vf}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $\\dfrac{1}{u}$ is nonzero, take reciprocals to obtain\n\n$$u=\\frac{vf}{v-f}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-problem-5-part-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Briefly explain why $v\\ne f$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "If $v=f$, the denominator $v-f$ in part (a) would be zero.",
          "worked": "If $v=f$, the original equation gives $\\dfrac{1}{u}=\\dfrac{1}{f}-\\dfrac{1}{f}=0$. A reciprocal cannot equal zero, so $v\\ne f$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-problem-5-part-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Let $x_1=u-f$ and $x_2=v-f$. Show that $x_1x_2=f^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x_1x_2=f^2$.\n\nSubstitute the expression for $u$ from part (a), then simplify and cancel the nonzero factor $v-f$.",
          "worked": "Using part (a) and $v\\ne f$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x_1x_2&=(u-f)(v-f)\\\\x_1x_2&=\\left(\\frac{vf}{v-f}-f\\right)(v-f)\\\\x_1x_2&=\\frac{vf-f(v-f)}{v-f}(v-f)\\\\x_1x_2&=vf-f(v-f)\\\\x_1x_2&=f^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
